## Why This Is Asked
Demonstrates ability to design private, language-aware ML inference at scale with strict data locality and per-tenant isolation. Tests routing logic, canary deployment strategies, and cross-language drift handling.

## Key Concepts
- SageMaker multi-model vs. per-language endpoints
- PrivateLink data residency and IAM isolation
- Canary rollouts and per-language versioning
- Model Registry + Pipelines for safe promotions
- Tenant-scoped storage and encryption

## Code Example
```javascript
// Language route resolver
function routeEndpoint(lang) {
  const map = {
    en: 'ep-en',
    fr: 'ep-fr',
    de: 'ep-de'
  };
  return map[lang] || 'ep-default';
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
Tests a practical, production-ready approach to multi-tenant inference, with per-tenant routing, canary risk controls, and drift/latency monitoring within a VPC-bound data-residency model.

## Key Concepts
- SageMaker Endpoint variants and traffic weighting
- Per-tenant routing and isolation
- PrivateLink data lake access
- Canary rollout and rollback triggers
- Drift and latency monitoring, autoscaling, and cost control

## Code Example
